    "chunk_text": "Formulating a new law for foster care\n\nPress briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)\n\n- It has been identified that there is currently no formal legal provision on foster care that covers all children in need of alternative care in Sri Lanka. Therefore, with the aim of implementing the concept of foster care (foster parenting), which is a family-based alternative care system that has become a timely need, the National Child Protection Authority has submitted a Concept Paper to establish a foster care mechanism. Through the said proposed mechanism, it is expected to implement the care programme under two main methods, namely the establishment of foster care and distance foster support. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Acting Minister of Women and Child Affairs to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to introduce a new law for foster care, based on the said Concept Paper, was approved by the Cabinet."
