    "chunk_text": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between the the Viet Nam Trade Promotion Agency and the Sri Lanka Export Development Board\n\nPress briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-28 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)\n\n- It has been proposed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding  between the Vietnam Trade Promotion Agency and the Sri Lanka Export Development Board to strengthen trade cooperation between Sri Lanka and Viet Nam. The MoU will provide space for a wide range of trade promotion activities, including the exchange of trade-related information and market intelligence, joint participation in trade fairs, exhibitions and promotional events held in both countries, and the organization of meetings between business delegations. It is expected that this cooperation will provide tangible market opportunities for processed foods, fisheries, apparel and value-added agriculture, in particular. The concurrence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism has been received for the draft MoU. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development to sign the relevant MoU between the Viet Nam Trade Promotion Agency and the Sri Lanka Export Development Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
