    "description": "Revisiting the Entitlements, Allowances and Privileges of the Members of Parliament, Ministers and Former Presidents",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12830",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-30 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Members of Parliament elected by the people, the Ministers and the former Presidents have been provided with different entitlements, allowances and privileges such as salaries, allowances, pensions, official quarters, vehicles, staff, office equipment, security personnel etc. The Government has to incur a considerable cost from the public taxes for the provision of said entitlements, allowances and privileges and it has been found the need to reduce this huge expenses within the existing fiscal space. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in her capacity as the Minister of Justice, Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils, Local Government and Labour to appoint a Committee with the following composition, to examine the matters in that regard and submit a Report with appropriate recommendations within two (02) months to limit the irrational entitlements, allowances and privileges which are causing an unnecessary burden to the General Treasury on a rational basis or to introduce other suitable alternative methodologies:\n\n*\tJustice K.T. Chitrasiri - (Chairman),\n\u00a0\u00a0\tRetired Judge of the Supreme Court;\n\n*\tMr. D. Dissanayake,\n\u00a0\u00a0\tRetired Ministry Secretary;\n\n*\tMrs. Jayantha C.T. Bulumulla,\n\u00a0\u00a0\tRetired District Secretary/Government Agent;",
