    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-08-26 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The harvesting of paddy in the Yala season 2024 has been started by now and the Cabinet has already granted approval to provide pledge loans to the small and medium - scale mill owners for upto a maximum of Rs.6,000 million through commercial banks to purchase paddy in the Yala season at a subsidized interest rate. The approval of the Cabinet has been granted to take action as follows, taking into consideration the proposals presented by the Hon. President and the Minister of Agriculture and Plantation Industries, with the aim of increasing the competitiveness of purchasing paddy and encouraging the paddy production in the upcoming Maha season.\n\n* \tProvision of Rs. 500 million to the Paddy Marketing Board to be able to actively participate in the Government's paddy buying programme in the Yala season 2024.\n\n*\tPurchase of Nadu paddy at Rs 105/- per kg, Samba paddy at Rs 115/- per kg and Keeri Samba paddy at Rs 130/- per kg by the Paddy Marketing Board.\n\n* \tIncreasing the fertilizer subsidy of Rs.15,000/- paid per hectare up to Rs.25,000/- per hectare, to encourage farmers to cultivate paddy, so that they can get a maximum yield in the upcoming Maha season.",
