    "date_str": "2024-07-22",
    "description": "Establishment of a Regulatory Institution in the Name of \"Films Sri Lanka\" \tinstead of the proposed \"National Films Development Commission\"",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12696",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal submitted to establish the \"National Films Development Commission\" to establish a new institutional framework enabling the National Film Corporation to move away from the current business activities and carry out regulatory-based activities, provide opportunities and facilities to enter the digital platform thereby moving the local cinema to the international arena, was taken up for discussion at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024\u201104\u201129. In this instance, it has been decided that all stakeholders in the film industry should be consulted and views be obtained regarding the proposal. Accordingly, it has been decided to replace the name of the \"National Films Development Commission\" with \"Films Sri Lanka\" based on the matters furnished at the discussion held with the relevant parties and to take into account the proposals presented at the said meeting in the preparation of the proposed Bill.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill for the establishment of \"Films Sri Lanka\" based on the above matters, was approved by the Cabinet.",
